Release signing keys
====================

This directory holds the OpenPGP public keys whose signatures the node scripts
accept on a telcoin-network release. setup-node.sh (--install-method release,
and Docker installs given a release tag) and update-node.sh download a
release's SHA256SUMS and SHA256SUMS.asc and run

    gpgv --status-fd 1 --keyring <every *.asc here, dearmored> SHA256SUMS.asc SHA256SUMS

They accept the release only when gpgv reports a good signature (GOODSIG then
VALIDSIG) whose primary key fingerprint belongs to one of these files, and no
line reports BADSIG, EXPKEYSIG, REVKEYSIG, NO_PUBKEY, ERRSIG or EXPSIG. Then
every file used from the release (the tarball, IMAGE_DIGEST) must match its
SHA256SUMS line, and the chain-config lines must carry the hashes these scripts
pin. Nothing from a release that fails a check is installed or run.

Format
------

One ASCII-armored public key per file, named <github-handle>.asc, the same
files as .github/maintainer-gpg-keys/ in the telcoin-network repository on
main. Every *.asc file here is read; other files (this README) are ignored. A
key that is expired or revoked stays refused even while its file is here.

Adding or removing a key
------------------------

1. Take the key from .github/maintainer-gpg-keys/<handle>.asc on the
   telcoin-network main branch, and check its fingerprint against the
   maintainer release keys table in that repository's SECURITY.md and
   against https://github.com/<handle>.gpg:

       gpg --show-keys --with-fingerprint <handle>.asc

2. Add (or delete) lib/release-keys/<handle>.asc in tn-node-deployment and
   list it in update-scripts.sh SCRIPTS so the updater ships it.

3. Publish a signed script release. Hosts pick the key set up with
   update-scripts.sh; the keys are part of the signed MANIFEST, like the
   scripts that read them.

A release signed only by a key that is not here yet is refused until the
script release that carries the key is installed. A release whose
SHA256SUMS.asc also carries a signature by a key that is not here is refused
as well (NO_PUBKEY): add every signer's key before that release is installed.

While this directory holds no *.asc file, every release download is refused.
